    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d877">

                <pb facs="1173" n="1159" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg1159"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.2222 (1940)/11–1344</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wei</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to your note of
                    August 29 in regard to a military service agreement between China and the United
                    States. <pb facs="1174" n="1160" xml:id="pg1160"/> It is noted that the United
                    States Government now proposes that the military service agreement between China
                    and the United States include a stipulation that the agreement is not applicable
                    to Chinese nationals who have declared their intention of becoming American
                    citizens.</p>
                <p>In this connection, I wish to refer to the lettered paragraph (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">c</hi>) in your note of November 6, 1943, which
                    contained the above stipulation in substantially the same form, and my note of
                    May 11, 1944, in which I informed you that my Government accepted the reciprocal
                    military service agreement together with the various stipulations enumerated in
                    your note of November 6, 1943.</p>
                <p>In view of this fact, I wish to confirm that the agreement is not applicable to
                    Chinese nationals who have declared their intention of becoming American
                    citizens.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wei Tao-ming</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">[<placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-13">November 13,
                            1944</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
